	quest.7F170DC0480BDA16.title: "&dSpecial Boots!"
	quest.7F488072500E4F1C.quest_desc: [
		"This is the &6initial functional block&r to use for getting started, which is needed for creating &6Simulated Contraptions&r. "
		""
		"When it's activated, blocks connected through either super glue or honey glue will turn into a &6Physics Contraption&r (also known as a sublevel) which can move and rotate around in the world."
		""
		"Physics assemblers can be activated by &6Players and Deployers&r, holding right-click on the placed block will bring up a simple GUI with a movable indicator, used to set &6assembly or disassembly&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The physics assembler can be used on &6Physics Contraptions&r for disassembly, causing the contraption to quickly attempt to align itself to Minecraft's block grid. "
		""
		"If the contraption is able to align, it will convert back into regular blocks and if it cannot align to the grid or is too far from the ground, the disassembly will fail and the contraption will remain a physics object."
		""
		"When a Contraption is physically split, each half will split into its own &6Physics Contraption&r."
	]
	quest.7F488072500E4F1C.quest_subtitle: "Initial block to getting started"
	quest.7F488072500E4F1C.title: "&6Physics Assembler"
	quest.7F7642DC1C2D0C71.quest_subtitle: "Knightmetal Sword: 7 Attack Damage"
	quest.7F7642DC1C2D0C71.title: "Knightmetal Tools"
	quest.7F8B45AB658A5EA5.quest_desc: [
		"Never heard about the &dParadise Lost&r before?"
		""
		"I'm gonna say this is not the &bAether&r we all know, this is the &dParadise Lost&r, so it's a very similar place."
		""
		"To build the portal it's pretty easy, you need to find some &6Calcite&r and build the portal frame, once it is done, you're gonna need a bunch of &6Healing Splash Potion&r and throw it on the portal frame and you will turn the Calcite into &6Bloomed Calcite&r."
		""
		"To light up you need a simple water bucket."
	]
	quest.7F8B45AB658A5EA5.quest_subtitle: "Trust me this is not the Aether"
	quest.7F8B45AB658A5EA5.title: "&dA Lost What? Paradise Lost?"
